From 9fd97ff6a45accc621b0a30031512cd38cf10e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:24:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] MT-E1b: Motor Test -- motor IO lamps, HOME/Loop button
 state, loop count; Reload Motor Data drops HomeFlag

From the read-only audit of every Motor Test control (20260925):
- ALed1..10 were never wired. Runtime now carries state.led, decoded from the monitor's raw motionIO exactly as
  golden TMyEtherCatMotor::ScanMotorStatus (Motor/myEthercatmotor.cpp:1166-1189): CW=LMT-, HOME=ORG, CCW=LMT+,
  EMG, Alarm=ALM|ERROR_STOP, Soft CW/CCW=SLMT_P/N, Servo On=SVON; S Alarm / InPos stay false as golden shows them.
  null when the row has no sample (lamp = unknown, not off).
- SAFETY: reloadMotorData zeroed coordinates but left HomeFlag set, so Go/Loop interlocks passed on meaningless
  coordinates. Golden runs InitialMotorParameter() first, which sets HomeFlag=0 for every motor
  (cinitial.cpp:3615/:3773/:3989). New backend call GoldenClearAllHomeFlags(), called BEFORE zeroing.
- HOME / Loop Move jobs are published per motor (motion.homeJob / loopJob / loopCount) so the page can pop the
  buttons up when C++ ends the job (golden Timer1Timer :962-966) and show lblLoopCount (golden dwLoopCount).

Tests: WebMotorAccess 196/0 (new: HomeFlag cleared before zeroing), MotorPoints_HT9050 passed (led decode,
null led without sample, job fields); production_audit 0 changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
